Subject: [PATCH] daemon: pin Home Assistant Core startup on RK3399

AWS-LC CPU jitter seeding may abort on the Cortex-A72 cluster. Start
Core on Cortex-A53 CPUs, then restore the available CPU set after one
minute and once the Core Unix listener is reachable when configured.
Use the task spec to apply the temporary mask before Core can run,
and avoid persisting it as a user-configured Docker CPU limit.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/aws/aws-lc/issues/3604

diff --git a/daemon/start.go b/daemon/start.go
--- a/daemon/start.go
+++ b/daemon/start.go
@@ -179,6 +179,8 @@
 		return errdefs.System(err)
 	}
 
+	releaseStartupAffinity := daemon.pinRK3399CoreStartup(ctx, container, spec)
+
 	if resetRestartManager {
 		container.ResetRestartManager(true)
 		container.HasBeenManuallyStopped = false
@@ -257,6 +259,9 @@
 	container.State.SetRunning(ctr, tsk, startupTime)
 	container.HasBeenStartedBefore = true
 	daemon.setStateCounter(container)
+	if releaseStartupAffinity != nil {
